M05_Triangle_Tank and M05_Cathedral_Apache fill their fire_loc target-id
tables only in Created(). Neither table was registered for auto-save (the
Apache line was commented out), so after a load the timers pick a target id
from uninitialized memory and Find_Object() returns NULL or an unrelated
object. Register both tables with unused id 2 (12 and 40 bytes, under the
250-byte limit). New games are unchanged; a load restores the authored ids.
Saves made before this patch carry no id 2 and behave as before.

--- a/Mission05.cpp
+++ b/Mission05.cpp
@@ -1704,6 +1704,8 @@
 	{
 		
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( attacking, 1 );
+		// Vita save/load: fire_loc is only filled in Created().
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( fire_loc, 2 );
 	}
 
 	void Created (GameObject * obj)
@@ -6129,7 +6131,8 @@
 	REGISTER_VARIABLES()
 	{
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( apache_id, 1 );
-//		SAVE_VARIABLE( fire_loc, 2 );
+		// Vita save/load: fire_loc is only filled in Created().
+		SAVE_VARIABLE( fire_loc, 2 );
 		SAVE_VARIABLE( attacking, 3 );
 	}
 
